const body = `<h1>3.3c — Combat Round Resolver: Who Goes First?</h1>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity expand-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Expand Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Initiative Resolver</h3>
        <p>In tabletop RPGs, combat order is determined by an initiative roll. The highest roll goes first. Build a system that compares two initiative rolls and determines the combat order.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>InitiativeResolver</code>. Hardcode two <code>int</code> values: <code>playerRoll</code> and <code>enemyRoll</code> (values from 1-20).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Rules</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>If playerRoll > enemyRoll: player goes first. Print the turn order.</li>
            <li>If enemyRoll > playerRoll: enemy goes first. Print the turn order.</li>
            <li>If they're tied: compare a <code>int playerDex</code> and <code>int enemyDex</code> — higher dex wins the tie.</li>
            <li>If STILL tied after dex: flip a coin (use Math.random() > 0.5) — heads means player wins.</li>
            <li>Print the full resolution: who rolled what, who had higher dex, and who goes first.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Edge Cases</h3>
        <p>What happens if both players roll the same AND have the same dex? Does your tiebreaker work? Test it with matching values.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-03/boolean-logic.html">Booleans &amp; if Statements</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/math-class.html">Math.random()</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
